{{Quote|Sergeant, why are you so certain no one is coming?''"<br />"''We're just clones, sir. We're meant to be expendable.|Plo Koon and Clone Sergeant Sinker|<ref name="Rising Malevolence" />}}
'''Sinker''' was a [[Clone Sergeant]] who served in the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] during the [[Clone Wars]] along with the rest of Wolfpack throughout the conflict. He served as a sergeant under [[Jedi Master]] [[Plo Koon]] and [[Wolffe|Commander Wolffe]] in the [[104th Battalion]].

==Biography==
===Creation===
Like all of his fellow [[clone trooper]]s in the [[Grand Army of the Republic|Grand Army]] of the [[Galactic Republic]], Sinker was created as a [[Cloning|clone]] of the [[bounty hunter]] [[Jango Fett]] on the [[planet]] [[Kamino]].<ref name="TCW Encyclopedia" /> Sinker was made a [[Clone Sergeant|sergeant]] in the [[104th Battalion]], also known as the Wolfpack Battalion. The [[battalion]] was led by [[Clone Commander]] [[Wolffe]] and the Jedi Master and [[Jedi General|General]] Plo Koon,<ref name="Rising Malevolence" /> who served on the [[Jedi High Council]].<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref>

===Infiltrating the Nexus===
[[File:WolfpackReady-TCWBattleTales2.png|thumb|left|250px|Sinker and the Wolfpack prepare to infiltrate the Nexus.]]
Early on in the [[Clone Wars]], Sinker joined Wolffe, [[Boost]], and [[Clone Corporal]] [[Comet (clone trooper)|Comet]] to infiltrate the [[Nexus]], a floating city and trading outpost that was controlled by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatists]]. However, they were discovered by [[Wat Tambor]], who destroyed the city. Despite their failure, they managed to rescue [[Orkle|civilian]] and were rescued by Koon.<ref name="Battle Tales 2">[[Star Wars Adventures: The Clone Wars – Battle Tales 2|''Star Wars Adventures: The Clone Wars – Battle Tales'' 2]]</ref>

===Hunting the Malevolence===
{{Quote|Don't look at me. It's Boost, sir. He only takes a bath when he's on leave.|Sergeant Sinker to General Plo Koon on Boost|<ref name="Rising Malevolence" />}}
[[File:SinkerWorksonPod-RM.png|thumb|right|250px|Sinker works to repair their damaged escape pod.]]
During the hunt for the Separatist [[superweapon]] ''[[Malevolence]]'', Sinker escaped Jedi General Plo Koon's [[Triumphant|Jedi Attack Cruiser]] in a [[Republic escape pod]] along with [[Commander]] Wolffe, Boost, and Jedi Master Plo Koon [[Gender|himself]] after the [[cruiser]] was hit by an [[ion cannon]], wiping out all its power and leaving it defenseless. When their [[escape pod]] was attacked by several [[B1-series rocket battle droid|rocket battle droids]] and their [[Droch-class boarding ship|pod hunter]], Koon led the [[sergeant]] and Boost in successfully defending their pod long enough for [[General]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Jedi Commander|Commander]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] to rescue them, resulting in the Republic gathering enough intel on the [[Starship|ship]] from the survivors to destroy the ''Malevolence''.<ref name="Rising Malevolence" />

===Battle on Felucia===
Further on in the war, Sinker and the rest of the Wolfpack fought alongside Ahsoka Tano in a stealth mission to scale the walls of a Separatist outpost on [[Felucia]], during which Tano was captured by the [[Trandoshan]] hunter, [[Lo-Taren]]. In an attempt to find his missing padawan, General Anakin Skywalker sent Sinker and a few other members of the Wolfpack to search the area surrounding the outpost for his padawan. However, after several unsuccessful searches, they eventually left.<ref name="Padawan Lost">{{TCW|Padawan Lost}}</ref>

===Mission to Aleen===
[[File:Aleenmainframestation-MM.png|left|thumb|250x250px|Sinker and Boost with R2-D2 on the mainframe station.]]
On their first mission in their [[Phase II clone trooper armor|Phase II armor]], Sinker and the rest of Wolfpack was sent to the planet [[Aleen]] alongside [[R2-D2]] and [[C-3PO]] to aid the residents after several earthquakes. Boost and Sinker accompanied R2-D2 to the Aleen mainframe station where R2 downloaded republic tools onto their computers. After R2 had successfully began the download, the two clones returned to aid their Commander. When leaving the planet, Wolffe told Sinker and Boost they would leave the droids with Jedi General [[Adi Gallia]], something Sinker was very pleased to hear.<ref name="Mercy Mission">{{TCW|Mercy Mission (episode)}}</ref>

===Searching Oba Diah moon===
{{Quote|Wait. I think I found something. It's very faint, sir.''"<br />"''That is it.|Sinker and Plo Koon|<ref name="The Lost One" />}}
[[File:Sinker-TLO.png|thumb|250px|Sinker locates Shuttle 775519, flanked by Commander Wolffe and General Plo Koon.|alt=]]
Sinker continued to serve in the Wolfpack under General Plo Koon and Commander Wolffe during a [[Mission to Oba Diah (Clone Wars)|mission]] to the [[Oba Diah moon|moon]] of [[Oba Diah]]. In response to a [[distress signal]] originating from [[775519|Jedi T-6 shuttle 775519]], the Jedi Council dispatched Koon and the 104th Battalion to investigate.<ref name="The Lost One">{{TCW|The Lost One}}</ref> Sinker<ref name="Sinker subtitle The Lost One">{{TCW|The Lost One}} subtitles {{C|[[:File:SinkerAttribution-TLO.png|Image]]}}</ref> operated the scanners of a [[HAVw A6 Juggernaut|clone turbo tank]] and pinpointed the shuttle's location after receiving a faint signal in the midst of a heavy [[sandstorm]]. It was discovered that the shuttle was that of the late Jedi Master [[Sifo-Dyas]].<ref name="The Lost One">{{TCW|The Lost One}}</ref>

===Legacy===
{{Quote|The wolves! You got your Wolfpack back!''"<br />"''Yeah. They fight just like the boys.|Gregor and Wolffe during the Battle for Lothal|<ref name="A Fool's Hope">{{Rebels|A Fool's Hope}}</ref>}}
Sinker was later mentioned by Wolffe in an entry in the survival compendium "[[Neyo's Almanac of Clankers]]," which described their [[mission to Quarmendy]].<ref name="Official Magazine 118">{{GermanFanCite|118|Database}}</ref> In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="A Fool's Hope date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[A Fool's Hope]]" to [[1 BBY]].</ref> Wolffe and former [[clone commando]] [[Gregor]] fought in the [[Liberation of Lothal]] from the [[Galactic Empire]]. During the conflict, Lothal's native [[Loth-wolf|loth-wolves]] joined the fight against Imperial forces. Observing the similarity between the wolves and the "Wolfpack" nickname for his squad in the 104th Battalion, Gregor commented that Wolffe had his Wolfpack back. Wolffe responded that they fought just like Sinker and his other men.<ref name="A Fool's Hope" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:Sinker-SWZ.png|thumb|left|300px|Sinker piloting an ARC-170 starfighter being pursued by vulture droid starfighters.]]
Like most clones of Jango Fett, Sinker stood at 1.83 [[meter]]s (6 [[Foot|feet]]) tall,<ref name="TCW Encyclopedia" /> with tan skin and brown eyes. However, his hair was gray. Sinker was known to have a sense of humor and cracked jokes even in the most dire circumstances. He also expressed some skill in mechanics when he helped rewire his escape pod after it had lost power due to the Malevolence's ion weapon.<ref name="Rising Malevolence" />

==Skills and abilities==
Sinker showed proficiency with a [[jetpack]] when he used one to scale the walls of a Separatist outpost on Felucia<ref name="Padawan Lost" /> as well as when he used one on [[Kadavo]].<ref name="Escape from Kadavo">{{TCW|Escape from Kadavo}}</ref> He was a capable pilot, flying an [[Aggressive ReConnaissance-170 starfighter]] on at least one occasion.<ref name="ARC-170">{{FFGXW2|set=ARC-170 Starfighter Expansion Pack|cardname="Sinker"}}</ref> Like so many other clones, Sinker became proficient in both armed and unarmed combat as well as military tactics.<ref name="TCW Encyclopedia" /> Sinker utilized these skills to great success as a sergeant in the Wolfpack, such as the hunt for the Malevolence<ref name="Rising Malevolence" /> and the Battle of Felucia, destroying many droids in the process.<ref name="Padawan Lost" />

==Equipment==
[[File:Sinker-CTRaF.png|thumb|right|180px|Sinker in his Phase II armor]]
Sinker wore [[Phase I clone trooper armor]] while hunting the Malevolence and during the fighting on Felucia.<ref name="Rising Malevolence" /><ref name="Padawan Lost" /> By the time of the earthquakes on Aleen, he was equipped with Phase II clone trooper armor.<ref name="Mercy Mission" /> Sinker stylized both types of his armor with Wolfpack symbols.
Sinker utilized a jetpack to scale vertical surfaces on several missions.<ref name="Padawan Lost" /> Throughout the [[Clone Wars]], Sinker used the [[DC-15A blaster carbine]].<ref name="Rising Malevolence" />

==Behind the scenes==
Sinker, like the rest of the clone troopers, was portrayed by [[Dee Bradley Baker]] in the animated TV series, [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]].<ref name="Rising Malevolence" /> Throughout the series, Sinker's character model changed three times.

